Package: mcommander
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ${perl:Depends}
Recommends: mcommander-plugins, mcommander-lua, groff-base, man-db, python3
Suggests: libx11-6, libaspell15 | libhunspell-1.7-0, universal-ctags
# mc6 was an earlier name of this program, published in a PPA of its own and
# retired. The two share one path, /usr/bin/mctree, which this package takes
# over; they can otherwise be installed together, so no Conflicts is needed.
Replaces: mc6
Description: twin-panel text-mode file manager with loadable panel plugins
 M-Commander is a twin-panel text-mode file manager based on GNU Midnight
 Commander.  Its architecture is built around a compact core and dynamically
 loaded panel plugins.  The plugins provide a uniform panel interface for
 archives, remote file systems, repositories, and other data sources.
 Commands are run in a built-in terminal.  M-Commander also includes a text
 editor with syntax highlighting and a viewer that supports both text and
 binary formats.
 .
 It installs /usr/bin/mcommander and the mc6, mcedit6, mview, mcdiff6 and mctree
 symbolic links, so it can be installed beside the mc package.
 .
 The mcommander-plugins package adds panels for archives and for files on
 remote systems.  The mcommander-lua package adds the features written in Lua.

Package: mcommander-plugins
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         mcommander (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests: git, docker.io, openssh-client
Description: archive and remote system panels for M-Commander
 Panel plugins that M-Commander loads at run time.  They open an archive or a
 remote system in a panel, so that its contents are handled like ordinary
 files: tar, zip and the other formats libarchive reads, FTP, SFTP, Samba, S3,
 Git, Docker, Kubernetes, MongoDB, SQLite, systemd units and shell links over
 ssh.
 .
 The Docker and Kubernetes panels talk to the docker and kubectl commands,
 which have to be installed separately.
 .
 The package also installs mcstruct, which shows a binary file as a tree of
 named fields.

Package: mcommander-lua
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         mcommander (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends: chafa, poppler-utils
Suggests: libsixel-bin, binutils, imagemagick, exif
Description: Lua runtime and scripts for M-Commander
 The Lua runtime plugin that M-Commander loads at run time, and the scripts
 that come with it: pictures in the terminal through sixel or chafa, markdown
 and PDF in the viewer, and readable views of dBase tables and ELF binaries.
 .
 Without this package M-Commander runs, and the features written in Lua are
 absent.
